description.narrative:
Outcome 1: Grant­making and Resourcing 
­- Strengthened governance and operations among 100+ LGBTIQ+ organisations globally;

Outcome 2: Capacity Strengthening and Technical Assistance 
-­ Increased national and regional self­determination and collaboration;

Outcome 3: Increasing Opportunities and Resources for Advocacy 
-­ Greater access to civic and political space by marginalised LGBTIQ+ populations;

Outcome 4: Movement Building, Coalition Strengthening and Collective Learning ­
- Durable cross­-sector alliances to counter authoritarianism and anti­-rights attacks. This movement strengthening strategy builds collective power by investing in communities’ capacity to organise, protect themselves, and lead sustained systemic transformation
